# ratified 2026-07-23), captured as a patch artefact by owner card
# (2026-07-23 ~14:35, via Director) instead of live working-file state.
#
# Why a patch, not live code: the type system correctly refuses the
# guidance-data listing of a tool with no definition — AllToolName's
# AggregatedToolName leg carries a bidirectional satisfies guard in
# universal-tools/definitions.ts demanding a full tool definition
# (description + inputSchema). Listing the tool is transitively
# "implement the tool", which is MCP-121's own build deliverable.
# Until then the sketch cannot sit green in the tree.
#
# Owner ruling folded in (card 2026-07-23 ~14:22): get-agent-rules-and-guidance
# takes callOrder 0 ("call order 0 is a special case, it makes it almost
# certain the agent will read the instruction"); get-curriculum-model
# shifts to 1. Test descriptions updated to match.
#
# Base sha: 36b94f280268f5b5a6f2411927fb4649a249566e (coordination/estate-2026-07)
# Contains: new tool metadata entry + callOrder assignments +
# .toSorted refactors + prerequisite-guidance re-export reshuffle +
# guidance-data listing + updated test descriptions.
# Pickup: the MCP-121 build phase. Expect to implement the tool
# definition/handler to make the guidance-data hunk compile.
